# What never enters the build context.
#
# The working tree is about 1GB, and almost all of it is either rebuilt
# inside the image or never served. Everything listed here is excluded
# before the daemon is handed anything, which is what keeps the context
# at roughly the size of public/.

# Rebuilt in the image. Copying the host's would also drop a macOS
# arm64 node_modules into a Linux image, where the SWC binary is wrong.
node_modules
.next
out
build
.swc

# 209MB of history, and nothing in the image reads it.
.git
.gitignore

# Reference recordings for the demo panels. Already gitignored; they are
# named here too so a fresh clone that still has them does not ship them.
*.mov

# Source artwork, not served. public/brand carries the derived files.
brand
New BG asset

# The documentation generators and their GitBook. The site image does not
# serve them: the compose "docs" service mounts this folder from the host
# instead, so the previewer always reads what is actually on disk.
product-docs

# Written but unpublished routes. Outside pages/, so Next does not build
# them, but there is no reason to send them either.
page-drafts

# Docker's own files, and local tooling.
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
DOCKER.md
.claude
.agent

# Local environment and editor noise.
.env*.local
.vercel
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
coverage
*.pem
*.tsbuildinfo
